  "notes": "Four existing-run routes are now traced: stream, status update, cancel, and delete. Redis replay uses the run selected by the ownership-checked database query. Last-Event-ID selects a position in that run’s buffer; even an unrecognized cursor cannot select another run. ([raw.githubusercontent.com](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aegra/aegra/d7d80c850010a9c5a3d2be59254c19b9eb0e25dd/libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py)) Status update and cancel check the run, thread, and caller before signaling the broker; delete repeats all three checks in the DELETE itself. ([raw.githubusercontent.com](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aegra/aegra/d7d80c850010a9c5a3d2be59254c19b9eb0e25dd/libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py)) Next: distinguish checkpoint identifiers used by persistence from those merely serialized in responses."
}

